---
// Goal: show that Jev from TypeSafe answers by default, with its address, key variable and model, and how to check it.
import SidePage from '../../layouts/SidePage.astro';
import Terminal from '../../components/Terminal.astro';
import BackendFacts from '../../components/BackendFacts.astro';
import { BACKEND_PAGES, BACKENDS_SEE, KEY_VARIABLE } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
import { captioned } from '../../data/samples.mjs';
import { backend } from '../../lib/backends-table.mjs';
import CheckLines from '../../components/CheckLines.astro';
import FromYourLanguage from '../../components/FromYourLanguage.astro';

const page = BACKEND_PAGES.find((p) => p.slug === 'typesafe');
const b = backend('typesafe');
const [one, lines, plan] = captioned('install/backends/typesafe', BACKENDS_SEE.typesafe);
---
<SidePage pages={BACKEND_PAGES} page={{ ...page, description: 'Jev from TypeSafe, the backend ThinkThen asks by default: its address, key variable, model, and check.' }} name="Models">
  <h1>TypeSafe Jev</h1>
  <p class="lede">Jev is TypeSafe's decision model. ThinkThen asks it when you name no backend.</p>

  <BackendFacts name="typesafe" />
  <p>The default model is a pinned version. TypeSafe can move an alias to a new model, and the pinned version stays the same. Name another version with <code>--model</code> only when you mean to change the model behind a run.</p>
  <p>On 2026-10-05, the <a href="https://github.com/botassembly/thinkthen-exp/tree/7c8197b5/experiments/0033-jev-in-your-database">0033 database report</a> recorded Jev 1.13.0 at $0.042 per million input tokens, with free output. Check your account terms for the rate you will pay.</p>

  <h2>Two ways to reach it</h2>
  <p>With no backend named, ThinkThen posts to the same address with the same model and reads the key from <code>{KEY_VARIABLE}</code>. With <code>--backend {b.name}</code>, it reads the key from <code>{b.keys[0]}</code>. Both reach the same model, and both share the answer cache.</p>
  <Terminal run={one} caption={one.see} />
  <Terminal run={lines} caption={lines.see} />

  <h2>Check it</h2>
  <p><code>thinkthen backends check</code> sends four fixed test questions, then one small call through each of the ten functions. It reports which inputs the backend can answer. The plan shows where they would go.</p>
  <Terminal run={plan} caption={plan.see} />
  <CheckLines name="typesafe" />

  <FromYourLanguage />

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/models/">All models</a> · <a href="/start/configuration/">Configuration</a></p>
</SidePage>
